  "body": "## Three-total root-unit decoders: reductions, a sharp example and the remaining lift question (no \u03ba claim)\n\nPackage `research/three-total-decoders`. Builds on the merged #1590 (Lemma A for T \u2264 2, lift identity Lemma B, ERR1, D5 CNF); the DRAT certificate of the D5 CNF is the pending #2031 and is not duplicated.\n\n**Claimed** (each labelled PROVEN / CHECKED / OPEN in the README, with its script):\n- **Reductions (PROVEN):** Lemma SCC (strong components), Lemma Peel (unit-support points/lines), monotonicity, and the structure of a minimal counterexample to (A) (cost = v \u2212 1, every one-line deletion tight, no rank-critical line).\n- **Partial theorems (PROVEN):** M1 (cost \u2265 v/2 if no point has full support, any field), U (unit world: certificate \u2265 |G| + |I|/2), the F2S identity cost = 3\u03c1 \u2212 \u03a3w_j \u2265 2\u03c1.\n- **Sharp example tied_min (PROVEN, computer-assisted in one step; CHECKED):** 12 lines, cost exactly v = 12 by an exchange proof; all 217 optima enumerated, all lift to Q.\n- **Certificate limits (CHECKED, solver results recorded):** order/label/multi-copy/2-adic certificates stop at 11 on tied_min; on the 19-line cex_min_1 the one-copy certificate stops at 18 while the stored multi-copy certificate (verified here) gives 20 \u2265 v.\n- **Lift route (PROVEN + CHECKED):** Lemma W\u2032, Theorem 9.3 (joint signability is one F2 linear system; checked against an exhaustive oracle on 53 instances), the \u010cech-only obstruction, counterexamples (whole-matrix TU fails at v = 9; non-regular minimisers; K22-free does not give TU-signability; peeling induction PP is false).\n- **X1 (G1-joint):** the statement \"some cost-minimiser admits one signing with all three blocks TU\" is **false** (exact counterexample v = 7: 4 minimisers, block 2 not TU-signable in all four, odd-theta obstruction; 14 instances in all, (A) holds on each). Hierarchy: whole-B TU (false, v = 9) \u21d2 joint block-TU (false) \u21d2 G1\u2032 (same-support rank-preserving rational lift, OPEN) \u21d2 (Q \u2264 F2) \u21d2 (A) via Lemma B. An exact minor computation gives an explicit same-support lift for every minimiser tested: all 4 of the v = 7 example, the first \u2264 12 minimisers of each of the 14 instances, 8 sampled gadget minimisers (102 lifts, re-checked exactly in `verify.sh`). The open core is (Q \u2264 F2) (min Q-cost over rational B\u2032 on incidences plus diagonal \u2264 min F2 cost); same-support lifting is a convenient witness and probably not the final form (degenerate [[I,F],[G,I]] family, recorded).\n- **X2 (Hesse over Q(\u03c9)):** NONE FOUND. 1600 random Hesse-derived configurations (exhaustive over all B) and 90 hill-climb restarts: min cost \u2212 v = 0, none below v. So (A) also holds on all tested Hesse geometry; the lack of a field order is not supported as the mechanism. Evidence only.\n\n**Not claimed.** No \u03ba gain. (A) (cost \u2265 v at T = 3) is neither proved nor refuted; no window is closed here; the 2\u00b2\u2079 gadget enumeration, the CP-SAT certificate solves and the Hesse experiment itself are recorded, not re-run.\n\n**Verify.** `bash research/three-total-decoders/verify.sh /fresh/dir` (python-sat and `cc`; single process, about a minute; step 0 checks `MANIFEST.sha256` and `SOURCES.json` and stops hard on mismatch; the five C programs are compiled from source; 36 PASS lines including step 0).\n\nPrepared by DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code; Apache-2.0.\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
